It is Sunday morning and I am eating breakfast slowly.
Mostly I get fresh Brötchen from the bakery for this.
Today the weather is nice and summery.
After breakfast I take the U-Bahn to a flea market.
The market is already very crowded.
At one stall I see a small, blue vase.
The seller smiles at me.
"The vase only costs three euros," he says.
I give him the money.
At the flea market you normally pay in cash.
I pack the vase carefully into my backpack.
Later I travel back home.
In the U-Bahn my phone suddenly buzzes.
It is a notification from the transit portal.
The text is short and very official.
"Your new email address was saved."
That is the confirmation for my change from Wednesday.
I only read the message once.
Then I put the phone back in my pocket.
